{"repositoryId":406174200,"availability":"available","full":"tlaplus-community/tlaplus-nvim-plugin","name":"tlaplus-nvim-plugin","description":"In-place translation of TLA⁺ symbols into Unicode, in Neovim","category":"Developer tools","language":"Lua","stars":15,"forks":2,"created":"2021-09-14T00:46:09Z","updated":"2026-10-17T21:39:23Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":[],"demo":"https://asciinema.org/a/620647","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T18:18:02.427Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T18:18:02.427Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T18:18:02.427Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-18T18:18:02.427Z","stars":15,"forks":2}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This is a TLA⁺ plugin for Neovim that translates ASCII TLA⁺ symbols into Unicode as you type. It translates \\leq into ≤, into ⇔, \\A into ∀, and so on. Watch the asciinema demo!","Upon opening a .tla file in nvim, around 80 different key mappings will be defined for the buffer. These mappings make it so whenever you type an ASCII TLA+ symbol, the ASCII will be replaced by its Unicode counterpart. The Unicode mappings follow the standardization proposal laid out here.","The TLA+ tree-sitter grammar is set up to highlight Unicode symbols identically to their ASCII counterparts. It pairs very nicely with this plugin; to get it, first install & configure nvim-treesitter then run :TSInstall tlaplus."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tlaplus-community/tlaplus-nvim-plugin/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"ed68cd5c549733392249a20402dc5eb2a1af64a7304eaed4c8f0bb8d7512b697","extractedAt":"2026-10-18T18:18:02.525Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T18:18:02.525Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"This is a TLA⁺ plugin for Neovim that translates ASCII TLA⁺ symbols into Unicode as you type. It translates \\leq into ≤, into ⇔, \\A into ∀, and so on. Watch the asciinema demo!","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tlaplus-com